WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.100
You are many things to many people.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.100
A familiar face at home.

3
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.760
A colleague at work.

4
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.400
A voice in a community.

5
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.580
Each relationship has its own context.

6
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.030
But online, those contexts can end up tied to a
single account.

7
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.660
One profile.

8
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.000
One provider.

9
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.890
One place deciding whether you can still be
reached.

10
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.990
When that account becomes unavailable,

11
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.250
more than a login can disappear.

12
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.130
Connections you depend on can disappear with it.

13
00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.610
PRP starts with your autonomy.

14
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.270
You can use different identities in different
relationships.

15
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.880
There is no requirement to place every part of
your life

16
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.010
under one universal identifier.

17
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.610
Each relationship has its own rules for
recognition and access.

18
00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.230
You choose which identities to use,

19
00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:57.660
which services to trust,

20
00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.570
and which contexts to keep separate.

21
00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.850
With continuity authorized,

22
00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:10.830
a new device or a different network need not
mean starting over.

23
00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.770
The path can change while the relationship
remains.

24
00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.950
Keeping contexts separate does not make every
trace invisible.

25
00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.300
Your identities.

26
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:22.960
Your relationships.

27
00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:24.600
Your choices.

28
00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.360
PRP.

